  "plain": "In the 1950s a Canadian named Wilbert B. Smith wrote a paper on how unknown craft might be propelled, and it was passed to Vannevar Bush, a top American government science adviser, for his view. The UFO researcher Grant Cameron says this comes from Smith's personal files, where Smith writes, in Cameron's words, that the UFO writer Donald Keyhoe \"took the document on the propulsion to Vannevar Bush and we're waiting for his opinion.\" If true, it would show such ideas reaching the very top of American science at the time."
